OL,3,GNEWSABoy, 12, who could not swim
OL,4,Adrowned after river current took hold
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 12-year-old boy who drowned in a
OL,7,Friver on a warm May day could not swim
OL,8,Fand may have been carried away from a
OL,9,Fshallow area by strong currents, an
OL,10,Finquest heard.
OL,12,FOlder teenagers tried to rescue Junior
OL,13,FSlater from the River Ribble in
OL,14,FRibchester, Lancashire, after friends
OL,15,Finitially thought his cries for help
OL,16,Fwere a joke, Preston Coroner's Court
OL,17,Fwas told.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,403,400,260,160,0,100
